.TH PTY_OPEN 3 2026-10-03 "libptytest 0.1" "libptytest Manual"
.SH NAME
pty_open, pty_close, pty_set_close_grace, pty_resize, pty_get_size,
pty_version \- create, size and destroy a PTY test session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <ptytest.h>
.PP
.BI "PtySession *pty_open(int " cols ", int " rows );
.BI "void pty_close(PtySession *" s );
.BI "void pty_set_close_grace(PtySession *" s ", int " ms );
.BI "int pty_resize(PtySession *" s ", int " cols ", int " rows );
.BI "void pty_get_size(PtySession *" s ", int *" cols ", int *" rows );
.B "const char *pty_version(void);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR pty_open ()
creates a session with a blank screen of
.I cols
columns and
.I rows
rows (each between 1 and 4096).
No process runs yet: start one with
.BR pty_run (3),
or feed bytes to the emulator directly with
.BR pty_feed (3).
.PP
.BR pty_close ()
ends the session.
A child that is still running is given the close grace period to exit by
itself, then is sent
.BR SIGTERM ,
then, if it has not exited within two seconds,
.BR SIGKILL .
The child is always reaped.
The master side of the PTY is closed and all memory is released.
.I s
may be NULL.
.PP
.BR pty_set_close_grace ()
sets the grace period in milliseconds; 0 (or a negative value) means none.
The default comes from the environment variable
.BR PTYTEST_CLOSE_GRACE_MS ,
read by
.BR pty_open (),
and is 0 when that is unset or malformed.
A grace period is wanted when the program under test writes something on
its way out that a signal would truncate \(em the
.I .gcda
files of a coverage build are the usual case.
It costs its full length for a child that never exits by itself.
.PP
.BR pty_resize ()
changes the window size.
Pending output is processed first, at the old size; then the kernel is
told the new size, which sends
.B SIGWINCH
to the child's foreground process group, and the screen is resized.
Content keeps its top-left position and is clipped; there is no reflow.
The scrolling region is reset and the cursor is clamped.
Without a running child only the screen is resized.
.PP
.BR pty_get_size ()
stores the current size in the non-NULL arguments (0 for a NULL session).
.PP
.BR pty_version ()
returns the library version, such as "0.1.0" or, between releases,
"0.1.0.12" (twelve commits past the tag).
.SH RETURN VALUE
.BR pty_open ()
returns the session, or NULL if the size is out of range or memory is
exhausted.
.BR pty_resize ()
returns 0 on success, \-1 on an invalid size or a failed
.BR ioctl (2).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PTYTEST_CLOSE_GRACE_MS
Default close grace period, in milliseconds.
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
PtySession *s = pty_open(80, 24);
const char *argv[] = { "./my\-tui", NULL };
if (pty_run(s, argv) != 0)
    perror("pty_run");
/* ... */
pty_resize(s, 100, 30);
ASSERT_WAIT_FOR(s, "100x30", 3000);
pty_close(s);
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pty_run (3),
.BR pty_wait_exit (3),
.BR libptytest (3),
.BR libptytest (7)
